//! Widening `hnf3`'s application residual.
//!
//! Three classes are supplied here, each with a non-vacuity witness computed
//! over the real reflected environment.
//!
//! # History, because it explains the shape
//!
//! This module originally also REFUTED the residual, at `app (bvar 0) (sort 0)`:
//! that term is stuck, and `nf_head` was uninhabited there because
//! `rigid_app_head` had no `bvar` arm and `iota_neutral` has none either. The
//! refutation and its two supports have been RETIRED, because
//! `rigid_app_head` now has that arm and the whole bvar-headed class falls to
//! the existing `hnf3_app_residual_of_rigid`.
//!
//! `bvarapp_wh3_stuck` survives and changes role: it was the stuckness half of
//! the counterexample, and is now the stuckness half of a positive witness for
//! the newly-covered class. `kapp_head_bvar_absurd` and
//! `iota_neutral_no_bvar_head` also survive — `iota_neutral` really does still
//! have no bvar arm; it is `rigid_app_head` that gained one.
//!
//! # What IS supplied here
//!
//! The chaining induction `hnf_conv.rs` named as missing, in both flavours:
//! `iota_neutral` holds all the way **up** a delta-dead spine, because its `app`
//! arm recurses and so a const-headed spine needs neutrality at every prefix.
//! Purely structural over the term, not over reduction — which is why it is
//! short. Three classes follow: delta-dead recmeta-free, under-applied, and
//! bvar-major, the last being the first `nf_head` witness at a
//! **recursor-headed** application anywhere in the tree.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The chaining inductions, three new suppliers, and the refutation.
    pub(super) fn add_hnf3_residual(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_IOTA_NEUTRAL_OF_DEAD_CONST_HEAD,
            "iota_neutral_of_dead_const_head: iota_neutral holds all the way UP a delta-dead recmeta-free spine. THE CHAINING INDUCTION the docs named as missing. \\
\\
iota_neutral's app arm recurses, so a const-headed spine needs neutrality at EVERY PREFIX, not just at the whole term. hnf_conv.rs recorded that this induction was not written; nothing chained iota_neutral up such a spine and the only witness in tree was at arity 1. It is purely STRUCTURAL over the term rather than over reduction, which is why it is short. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_APP_OF_DEAD_CONST_HEAD,
            "nf_head_app_of_dead_const_head: a delta-dead recmeta-free const-headed application has a normal-form head. Composes the chaining induction with iota_immune_of_dead_const_head. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HNF3_APP_RESIDUAL_OF_DEAD_CONST_HEAD,
            "hnf3_app_residual_of_dead_const_head: the residual, supplied for the delta-dead recmeta-free class. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_DEAD_CONST_SPINE_WITNESS,
            "nf_head_dead_const_spine_witness (NON-VACUITY): the class above is inhabited at ARITY 2, by computation over the real reflected environment. The pre-existing witness was arity 1, so this genuinely exercises the chaining. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_IOTA_NEUTRAL_OF_UNDER_APPLIED,
            "iota_neutral_of_under_applied: the same chaining for an UNDER-APPLIED recursor spine. The bound weakens downward along the spine, so every prefix is under-applied too — which is exactly the argument hnf_conv.rs said should work and had not been written. \\
\\
Under-applied is formally Le (list_length (kapp_args e)) MAJOR_IDX: iota_reduct reads the major by index, and the read is none when the spine is that short. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_APP_OF_UNDER_APPLIED,
            "nf_head_app_of_under_applied: an under-applied recursor-headed application has a normal-form head. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HNF3_APP_RESIDUAL_OF_UNDER_APPLIED,
            "hnf3_app_residual_of_under_applied: the residual, supplied for the under-applied recursor class. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_APP_OF_BVAR_MAJOR,
            "nf_head_app_of_bvar_major: a recursor spine whose major premise is a bound variable has a normal-form head. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HNF3_APP_RESIDUAL_OF_BVAR_MAJOR,
            "hnf3_app_residual_of_bvar_major: the residual, supplied for the bvar-major class. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_NATREC_UNDER_APPLIED_WITNESS,
            "nf_head_natrec_under_applied_witness (NON-VACUITY): the under-applied class is inhabited at the REAL reflected Nat.rec, whose RecMeta gives MAJOR_IDX 3, on a three-argument spine sitting exactly at the boundary. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_NATREC_BVAR_MAJOR_WITNESS,
            "nf_head_natrec_bvar_major_witness (NON-VACUITY): the first nf_head witness at a RECURSOR-headed application anywhere in the tree — the very class hnf was refuted at. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_HEAD_BVAR_ABSURD,
            "kapp_head_bvar_absurd: the Type-valued discriminator separating a bvar spine head from the rest. Type-valued deliberately, so the refutation below needs no LiftP. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_IOTA_NEUTRAL_NO_BVAR_HEAD,
            "iota_neutral_no_bvar_head: no iota_neutral has a bvar at its spine head. iota_neutral's two arms are const and app, and the app arm recurses to the head. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_BVARAPP_WH3_STUCK,
            "bvarapp_wh3_stuck: a bvar-headed application IS stuck under the three-way step, by the SAME single Eq.refl that proves wh3_rigid_app_is_stuck. reduce_app_head_red_wh3's bvar and sort arms are the same ilift string, and the iota chain short-circuits on the head having no const name. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

